 complaint about  where the overton window is  even for the loudest people shouting  free speech on the internet  they probably draw the line like most  people that say  endorsing pedophilia and oftentimes  people as a group  expressing their feelings that such and  such person has bad ideas and is dumb  is itself just people expressing their  own opinions should we  censor those people from criticizing  others this video  gives me this video gives me hope in  certain moments where i'm like this is  actually a pretty good video  and then it gives me brain cancer at the  same time probably not  the point is cries of censorship  directed at one side are often a smoke  screen for saying  my constitutive censorship is normal and  fine yours is not  case in points university professors  getting fired for their ideas  while the narrative is that the  censorious left is getting  anyone fired who doesn't fall in line  with their ideas independent reviews  actually show that while yes this does  happen it happens in  far greater numbers to left-leaning  professors at the hands of conservative  backlash  but back to the overton window there's a  bit of confusion over how it moves  a lot of popular thinking claims that  it's all on corrupt lawmakers who use  their power to intentionally shift the  window to the extreme  whether it's to be inflammatory or make  once fringe ideas more acceptable  and promote their own aims in a politico  interview  lehman argues that this is a  misconception while you can push the  window by advocating for radical ideas  he says it  actually happens through public  discourse he says this idea that  lawmakers are trying to shift the window  is absolutely false  lawmakers are actually in the business  of detecting where the window is  and then moving to be in accordance with  it others like noam chomsky  argue that some lawmakers have an  interest in keeping the overton window  where it is  and that they'll do a whole lot to make  sure people are 